  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda: Supporting Access to Justice for Sustainable Development in Uganda 2023-2028 (AJSD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To improve responsiveness and accessibility of gender-based violence (GBV) justice services. 2) To increase public access and utilization of commercial and land justice services. 3) To enhance availability and responsiveness of justice services by refugees and host communities. 4) To strengthen management, monitoring and evaluation systems for GBV, refugee response, commercial and land justice.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Families and households affected by GBV, business enterprises especially upcoming enterprises, and refugees. Indirect beneficiaries: The population at large including persons with disabilities and refugees in Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to secure a just society and sustainable development through improved people-centred justice services in Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
